<http://data.silknow.org/object/392454f2-c4f5-3711-9db7-dde925101825/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Tapestry woven silk and metal thread, lined with plain weave silk decorated with a metal thread tassel.\nThe cap is made from four triangular sections, identical in patterning.  On a green ground a zigzag band in white, originally silver strip wound around a white silk core, framing a triangle framed in white and decorated with trefoil shapes outlined n red, lozenges with black details.  In the centre of the green triangle four rows of small narrow oval white shapes outlined in red.\nSilk: green, S-twist; red, S-twist; black indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver strip open S-wound on white silk core.\nThe lining is green silk.\nThere is a drawstring around the base: two cords of yellow, white and green silk.\nThere is a tassel from the crown which is 13 cm long.\nThere is a fringe of doubled silver-gilt strip open S-wound on yellow silk and twisted to form a small eyelet at the crown."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/392454f2-c4f5-3711-9db7-dde925101825> .

